flowchart LR
  F[Foundations] --> S[Semantic tokens]
  S --> C[Components]
  F --> F1[Color]
  F --> F2[Type]
  F --> F3[Space]
  F --> F4[Shape]
  F --> F5[Motion]
  S --> S1[Surface]
  S --> S2[Content]
  S --> S3[Action]
  S --> S4[Status]
  C --> C1[Navigation]
  C --> C2[Control]
  C --> C3[Feedback]
  C --> C4[Container]
Rationale: foundations remain replaceable while semantic roles preserve consistency.
Quality gates: components use semantic tokens; role-based names are stable; contrast pairs are defined; spacing follows a scale; reduced-motion behavior is specified.
Examples: surface.default=#FFFFFF; surface.subtle=#F7F8FA; content.primary=#17202A; content.muted=#667085; action.primary=#315EFB; status.error=#B42318; space.1=4px; space.2=8px; radius.sm=6px; radius.md=8px.